FEATURE-097 is implemented as a complete vertical slice. Stopping here per the workflow.

## Summary

**Selected feature:** FEATURE-097 (must, deps satisfied) — *Login event listeners must filter by firewall (review C2)*. It also unblocks FEATURE-123.

**Root cause:** The stateless `api` / `admin_api` firewalls authenticate via bearer PAT but resolve principals from the same `app_users` / `app_admins` providers as the interactive firewalls. So `LoginSuccessEvent` / `LoginFailureEvent` fire on every API call, and the listeners' only guard (`instanceof User`/`Admin`) can't distinguish a real login from API traffic — producing spurious audit rows, login_history rows, phantom user_sessions, "new device" emails, and webhooks.

**What I did:**
- Added `src/EventListener/InteractiveFirewallTrait.php` — a shared allowlist guard (`['user','admin']` + `isInteractiveFirewall()`), keyed off `LoginSuccessEvent/LoginFailureEvent::getFirewallName()`.
- Applied the early-return guard to all five affected listeners: `AuditLogSecurityListener` (success+failure), `LoginHistoryListener`, `UserSessionListener`, `LoginNotificationListener`, and `WebhookListener` (success+failure — AC3 explicitly requires no webhook on failed API auth). `onLogout` handlers left untouched since stateless firewalls have no logout route.
- Added `tests/Functional/Security/ApiLoginSideEffectsTest.php` (2 tests, 8 assertions) covering AC2/AC3/AC5.

**Verification:**
- New tests pass; **confirmed meaningful** — with `src/EventListener/` stashed, both fail (audit-login +1, login.failure +1).
- Full `bin/verify-fast.sh`: **OK (419 tests, 1464 assertions), `=== All checks passed ===`**. No regressions; the only noise is the pre-existing Symfony 7.3 `eraseCredentials` deprecations. AC4 (interactive logins unchanged) is covered by the untouched, still-green LoginHistory/AuditLog/SessionManagement/LoginNotification/Webhook suites.

Per the workflow, I did **not** set `passes=true`, did **not** update `claude-progress.txt`, and did not commit — those await the reviewer pass.
