## Summary

Implemented **FEATURE-101** — *Invitation resend resurrects used invites; registered email not bound to invite* (review finding C6, priority **must**).

### The three defects fixed
1. **Web resend had no guard** — `AdminInvitationController::resend` regenerated any invitation unconditionally (`regenerate()` nulls `usedAt`), so a consumed invite could be resurrected and reused to create a second account in invitation-only mode.
2. **API resend guarded expiry but not used-ness** — a used-*and-expired* invite slipped the `!isExpired()` gate and got regenerated.
3. **Registration never bound the email** — `RegistrationController` captured the invited email for display only; any invite-link holder could register an arbitrary email.

### Changes
- **`AdminInvitationController::resend`** — reject when `isUsed()` (error flash + redirect).
- **`Api/AdminApiInvitationController::resend`** — reject when `isUsed()` (409). Removed the `!isExpired() → 409` branch that contradicted the web contract.
- **`RegistrationController::register`** — in invitation-only mode, reject when the POSTed email ≠ the invitation's email (case-insensitive); no user created, invite not consumed.
- **`templates/admin/invitations/list.html.twig`** — render `error` flashes.

### Drift reconciliation (AC2)
The web acceptance test (FEATURE-071 AC5) rotates a **non-expired** invite and expects success, while the API returned 409 for the same case — the pre-existing drift AC2 mandates eliminating. The used-ness guard is the real security fix; expiry-as-a-resend-blocker was the anomaly. I converged both surfaces on **"reject only when used"** and reconciled the API test `testResendNonExpiredInvitationReturns409` → `testResendNonExpiredUnusedInvitationRotatesToken`. Documented as **ADR-022**.

### Tests added
- Web: resend-used rejected (token unchanged, no email); mismatched-email registration rejected (no account, invite not consumed).
- API: resend-used returns 409 (token unchanged); reconciled non-expired-unused rotation test.

### Verification
`bin/verify-fast.sh` → **OK (429 tests, 1494 assertions), "=== All checks passed ==="**; anti-cheat scan clean. Only log noise is the pre-existing project-wide `eraseCredentials` deprecations.

Per the workflow I have **not** set `passes=true` in `feature_list.json` and **not** appended to `claude-progress.txt` — those await the reviewer pass. Stopping here after this one feature.
