The `config/reference.php` change is incidental auto-generated static-analysis drift (a `when@acceptance` env cache regeneration — same artifact FEATURE-096 noted excluding at commit time), not part of my logical change. Implementation is complete.

## Summary — FEATURE-098 (must): Deactivation / logout-everywhere must actually cut access (review C3)

Selected the only remaining `must`-priority feature with satisfied dependencies. Rewrote `.agent/SCRATCHPAD.md` for it, wrote tests, then implemented the smallest complete fix. `bin/verify-fast.sh` passes: **447 tests, 1590 assertions, "=== All checks passed ==="**.

### The two holes closed

**(a) Remember-me survived logout-everywhere.** The cookie's HMAC binds only identifier+expiry+password-hash, so dropping `user_sessions` rows didn't stop re-authentication.
- New explicit `User.sessionsInvalidatedAt` column (`migrations/Version20260706100000.php`, nullable → NULL treated as marker `0`, no behaviour change for existing rows).
- `ConfigAwareRememberMeHandler::computeHash` folds that timestamp into the HMAC → bumping it invalidates every outstanding remember-me cookie for the user at once, without touching the password.
- Web `AccountController::terminateAllSessions` and API `AdminApiUserController::forceLogout` now bump the marker + flush.

**(b) Stateless firewalls never rechecked account state.** A deactivated user's PAT / admin's token authenticated forever.
- `TokenAuthenticator` rejects (401) when the loaded User's `status !== 'active'` or `isLocked()`.
- `AdminTokenAuthenticator` rejects (401) when the loaded Admin is not `isActive()` (admins have no lockout column per ADR-021).
- API `deactivate` additionally drops sessions + `revokeAllByUserId` (PATs) + bumps the marker — active revoke as belt-and-suspenders.

### Tests — `tests/Functional/Security/DeactivationCutsAccessTest.php` (5 tests, all ACs)
Deactivated user PAT → 401 on `/api`; deactivated admin token → 401 on `/admin-api`; deactivate drops sessions + revokes PATs; remember-me dead after web logout-everywhere; remember-me dead after API force-logout.

One test-isolation note worth surfacing: in the full-suite run these tests initially failed because a leftover empty `remember_me.lifetime_days` config row makes `ConfigService::getInt()` return `0`, so the remember-me cookie expires immediately. I cleaned that key in the test (mirroring `RememberMeTest`), but the underlying "empty config value → 0 lifetime" is a real config-hygiene bug that belongs to FEATURE-120 (per-field config validation), not this feature.

