## Summary

**Feature:** Move email + webhook delivery off the login/request path to Symfony Messenger (review C9, priority `must` — the only remaining `must` with satisfied deps).

**What I did (all 7 ACs):**
- Installed `symfony/messenger` + `symfony/doctrine-messenger`.
- **`config/packages/messenger.yaml`** — Doctrine `async` transport with `retry_strategy` (exp. backoff) + `failed` failure transport; routes `SendEmailMessage` **and** `App\Message\SendWebhookMessage` → `async`. `when@test` routes email → `sync://` (so `MailerAssertionsTrait`, which counts *sent* not *queued*, keeps working) while `async` = `in-memory://` so a dispatched webhook message is inspectable. Acceptance override → `sync://` (no worker on the live server).
- **`SendWebhookMessage`** + **`SendWebhookMessageHandler`** (runs the HTTP + `WebhookDelivery` logging on the worker; throws on failure so Messenger retries → dead-letters).
- **`MessengerWebhookDispatcher`** now backs `WebhookDispatcherInterface` in prod/dev — all 4 call sites enqueue unchanged; the request never calls out itself.
- **`HttpWebhookDispatcher`** refactored to a single-attempt `send()`; removed the internal retry loop and the no-op **`backoff()`** (AC4); kept the static SSRF guard.
- **Migration** for `messenger_messages` (SQLite-compatible, DBAL-only table).
- **README** "Background worker" section documents the `messenger:consume async` requirement (AC6).
- **ADR-023** recorded in `DECISIONS.md`.
- **Tests:** new `tests/Functional/Messenger/AsyncDeliveryTest.php` (webhook message dispatched to the transport, not inline HTTP; email routed onto the bus + login still succeeds/notifies); reworked `WebhookDeliveryTest.php` to the new single-attempt + handler-throw semantics preserving `WebhookDelivery` logging assertions.

**Verification:** `bin/verify-fast.sh` → **`=== All checks passed ===`, OK (449 tests, 1592 assertions)** — PHPUnit + Codeception functional + live-server acceptance all green. The only log noise is pre-existing `eraseCredentials` deprecations. No skipped/weakened tests.

