## Summary

**Selected feature: FEATURE-114** — *Registration POST needs CSRF validation + rate limiting (review C21)* (priority `should`, no dependencies).

The registration POST had **no CSRF validation and no rate limiting** (the CSRF field FEATURE-007 once added was lost in later refactors), leaving `/register` open to CSRF-forged account creation and unthrottled account/email flooding — unlike every other auth POST, all already covered by `EndpointRateLimiter`.

### What I implemented
- **`templates/registration/register.html.twig`** — added the hidden `_token` = `csrf_token('register')` field (auto-included by the crawler/live forms, so existing form-based tests keep passing).
- **`src/Controller/RegistrationController.php`** — injected `EndpointRateLimiter`; at the top of the POST block, throttle keyed on client IP (`tooManyAttempts('register', $ip)`) sits **above** the CSRF check (ADR-016 fail-closed pattern), then `isCsrfTokenValid('register', …)`. Either gate re-renders the form with an error and creates no user, sends no email, writes no audit row.
- **NEW `tests/Functional/Registration/RegistrationSecurityTest.php`** — 2 behavioural tests: missing-CSRF POST is rejected with no user created (AC4); exceeding `rate_limit.max_attempts` blocks the 3rd registration *and* its verification email (AC5). Both genuinely fail against the pre-fix controller.
- **`tests/Functional/Security/PasswordPolicyTest.php`** — its 7 direct `/register` POSTs would otherwise now pass for the wrong reason (CSRF error) and one positive-path test would break, silently *weakening* policy coverage. Added a `registerPost()` helper that fetches a real token so these stay genuine policy tests, plus an `endpoint_rate_limits` cleanup to avoid cross-test throttle bleed.

### Verification
`bin/verify-fast.sh` → **OK (463 tests, 1648 assertions)**, `=== All checks passed ===` (PHPUnit + Codeception functional + live-server acceptance). Changed files are clean of anti-cheat patterns.

Per the required workflow, I have **not** set `passes=true`, **not** appended `claude-progress.txt`, and **not** committed — those await the reviewer pass.
