## FEATURE-102 — Kill ALL recovery tokens on deactivate OR delete + reject reset for inactive accounts (review C7 / ADR-020)

**Selected** because FEATURE-110 (its only dependency) is `passes=true`, and it's the natural security follow-on to the ADR-020 soft-delete work.

### The gap closed
A soft-deleted/deactivated account was blocked from *login* (UserChecker/AdminChecker), but its outstanding `password_reset_tokens`, `admin_password_reset_tokens`, and `magic_link_tokens` stayed valid, and the reset controllers never checked account status — so a pre-deactivation reset link could still set a fresh password.

### What was built
- **New `src/Security/RecoveryTokenInvalidator.php`** — autowired service with `invalidateForUser(email)` (kills unused password-reset + magic-link tokens) and `invalidateForAdmin(email)` (admin reset tokens), via bulk DQL mirroring the existing `invalidateOtherUnusedTokens` pattern.
- **Immediate kill wired into every inactive-transition** (no bypass, one line each after the status flush): user edit→inactive, user soft-delete (web + API), API deactivate, API PATCH→inactive; admin edit→inactive, admin soft-delete.
- **Consumption-time gate** (defense in depth, AC3/AC4) in `PasswordResetController::reset` and `AdminPasswordResetController::reset` — after token validity, resolve the account by email and reject with "no longer valid" (token=null) if null or inactive; covers both the GET form and POST submit.
- **New `tests/Functional/Security/RecoveryTokenInvalidationTest.php`** — 7 tests covering AC1–AC9.

### Verification
- New test: **7 tests, 18 assertions — OK**.
- Meaningfulness proven: disabling the invalidator → 5 invalidation tests fail; disabling the consumption gate → both AC3/AC4 tests fail.
- **`bin/verify-fast.sh`: OK (473 tests, 1688 assertions), "=== All checks passed ==="**, anti-cheat clean.

