## Summary

**Feature: FEATURE-113 — Apply the IP whitelist to magic-link login (review C20)**

The bug: `IpWhitelistListener` early-returned unless the authenticator was `FormLoginAuthenticator`, so `MagicLinkAuthenticator` was never IP-checked — a user restricted by `allowedIps` (or under a global `ip_whitelist.user_ips` policy) could log in from any IP by requesting a magic link, fully bypassing the whitelist.

**Changes**
- `src/EventListener/IpWhitelistListener.php` — the class guard now passes for both `FormLoginAuthenticator` **and** `MagicLinkAuthenticator`. Because the magic-link verify route is `/magic-link/verify` (not `^/admin`), it flows through the existing user-firewall branch, so global `ip_whitelist.user_ips` and the per-user `allowedIps` override (AC3) are both enforced with no other change. Added a comment documenting that `ImpersonationAuthenticator` (admin-initiated switch) and the API `TokenAuthenticator`/`AdminTokenAuthenticator` remain intentionally exempt (AC4).
- `tests/Functional/Security/MagicLinkIpWhitelistTest.php` (new) — 4 functional tests: whitelisted global IP succeeds; non-whitelisted global IP blocked (→ `/magic-link` + `.error` "not allowed", user left unauthenticated); per-user `allowedIps` restriction enforced; per-user override allows despite an excluding global policy.

**Verification**
- `MagicLinkIpWhitelistTest`: OK (4 tests, 18 assertions).
- Regression watch (`IpWhitelistTest`, `MagicLinkTest`, `TrustedIpTest`, `ImpersonateTest`): OK (22 tests, 70 assertions).
- `bin/verify-fast.sh`: OK (484 tests, 1737 assertions) — `=== All checks passed ===`.

All 5 acceptance criteria are covered. Remaining per the definition of done (deliberately not done yet): reviewer pass, `feature_list.json` evidence + `passes=true`, `claude-progress.txt` append, and commit.
