## Summary

Selected **FEATURE-120 — Admin config save must validate values per field type (review C28)**. No unmet dependencies; clean, self-contained slice. Implemented (not yet marked `passes=true`, progress log not appended, not committed — per the workflow).

**The bug (C28):** `AdminConfigController::save` wrote any submitted string for any config field with no validation, so `rate_limit.max_attempts=banana` persisted and silently coerced to `0` (= rate limiting disabled); out-of-set enums like `registration.mode=bogus` were likewise accepted.

**What I built:**
- **Enriched field declarations** across the 8 config pages so fields carry a *real* type/constraint (the "declared type" there was previously only `text`/`bool`): numeric fields → `int` with a `min` bound; closed-set fields → `enum` with `options` (`registration.mode`, `login_notifications.recognition_mode`, `email_verification.mode`, `2fa.enforcement` — each option set verified against its consuming code). Genuine free-form fields (webhook URLs, IP lists) stay `text`; URL/IP safety is out of scope (FEATURE-105 / the whitelist listener).
- **`src/Config/ConfigFieldValidator.php`** — pure, unit-tested service: rejects non-integers/negatives/out-of-range for `int`, out-of-set values for `enum`, non-canonical `bool`; passes `text`/unknown through.
- **`AdminConfigController`** — validates every *submitted* field; if any fails, persists nothing and re-renders the page (HTTP 422) with per-field errors and the admin's rejected input. Only fully-valid pages save + redirect. Partial POSTs no longer clobber untouched fields. Extracted a shared `renderConfig()` helper used by both `index()` and the failure path.
- **Template** — renders `.field-error` per field plus a summary banner.

**Tests (test-first):**
- `tests/Unit/Config/ConfigFieldValidatorTest.php` — int/enum/bool/text coverage incl. `banana`, `-5`, `1.5`, empty, out-of-set, min/max bounds.
- `tests/Functional/Admin/ConfigValidationTest.php` — AC4 (non-int `rate_limit.max_attempts` → 422 + field error + not persisted), out-of-set enum rejected, valid save still persists.

**Regression safety:** every existing controller-POST config test submits valid values, so all still 302-redirect and persist; the "validate only submitted fields" rule preserved the partial-POST tests (`AdminConfigTest`, `RegistrationModeTest`). No schema change, no new config key, no ADR (ties to the existing explicit/auditable design preference).

